// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_lcm_undeclared.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: engine/level/scene_dsl.emp's MANDATORY left-column policy — `scene()`'s
// guard (1) of the P3 Task 12 block: a scene attaching a per-column V-deform table
// (SceneVDeform.Columns) with `left_column_mask` left Undeclared fails the build.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "a scene with 1 layer(s) attaching a per-column V-deform table
// (SceneVDeform.Columns, sample speed 0, amplitude shift 2) declares NO left_column_mask
// policy" — the WHOLE interpolated signature, deliberately: sigil reports a comptime-fn
// ensure at the ENSURE's own span, not the call site, so the interpolated
// count/speed/shift triple is the only thing that names WHICH scene failed (the Task 12
// DONE block's discovery — it is what separated the six Rocking/Perspective elaborations
// in the natural-red run quoted in commit ba335e08). Matching the full triple is what
// keeps this case from passing on some OTHER scene's undeclared-policy diagnostic.
//
// THIS IS THE CASES ROW P3 TASK 12 EXPLICITLY LEFT TO TASK 15 (its DONE block, "Task 15
// note"). The guard went in with natural-red evidence — 192 failures across the six
// shipped per-column elaborations before their declarations existed — but that red
// predates the declarations and is not re-run by anything; this row is what keeps the
// guard's liveness checked on every canonical DEBUG build.
//
// TWO FIXTURES, ONE AUTHORED FIELD APART (the two-fixture differential, P1's mask-poison
// reference):
//
//   FIXTURE A — a one-layer locked scene attaching a per-column table, declaring
//               `left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Accept`. Accept is the REAL authored
//               answer both shipped per-column families use (Rocking because its
//               zero-table factor0 truth is comptime-invisible, Perspective because its
//               shimmer floor genuinely ships the artifact), so the control models the
//               shipped shape, not a convenient one. It must pass ALL FOUR lcm guards:
//               (1) declared, (2) declared WITH a subject, (3) not a Factor0Lock claim,
//               (4) not the refused SpriteMask. Its pass is MEASURED below by the
//               variant test on the constructed scene's own field.
//   FIXTURE B — byte-for-byte fixture A with the declaration REMOVED (the parameter
//               defaults to Undeclared, which is exactly how a real author forgets it).
//               Guard (1) fires.
//
// Expected `[Error]` count is 1: guard (2) passes for B (v-deform IS attached), guards
// (3)/(4) pass (Undeclared is neither), and every non-lcm guard is identical across the
// pair. A count of 2 means fixture A stopped being legal (Accept refused, or the
// no-policy-without-a-subject guard mis-widened); a count of 0 means the mandatory
// declaration went dead and a per-column scene can ship unadjudicated again.
//
// THE TABLE LABEL IS 0, the same spelling every scene poison uses (see
// poison_scene_own_caps.emp): the guard discriminates on the VARIANT, never the payload,
// and a real DeformTable_* name would tie this poison to another module's emission.
//
// THE GLOB IMPORTS ARE THE AUTHOR'S OWN SPELLING — see poison_scene_grid.emp's header.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_lcm_undeclared

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

// FIXTURE A — per-column table, policy declared. The shipped families' shape.
const POISON_LCM_SCENE_A: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Accept)

// FIXTURE B — byte-for-byte fixture A, declaration removed (defaults to Undeclared).
const POISON_LCM_SCENE_B: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2))

// ---- THE PASSING HALF (must stay green, and is MEASURED) ----
// The constructor is non-aborting either way, so "A passed" cannot be read off the build
// succeeding; it is read off A's OWN field carrying a declared policy — the exact
// predicate guard (1) tests — plus the diagnostic count above staying at 1.
ensure(scene_lcm_is_undeclared(POISON_LCM_SCENE_A.sc_left_col_mask) == 0,
       "poison_scene_lcm_undeclared: the CONTROL's left_column_mask reads as Undeclared — fixture A no longer declares the Accept policy, so the failing half below no longer isolates the missing declaration")

// ---- THE FAILING HALF — elaborating fixture B is what fires guard (1) ----
ensure(scene_lcm_is_undeclared(POISON_LCM_SCENE_B.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_undeclared: the poisoned fixture's left_column_mask no longer reads as Undeclared — the fixture stopped modelling the forgotten declaration and the expected diagnostic proves nothing")
